# People Domain Conventions

Rules for pipelines in the People domain (`dags/people/`).
Aligned with the People Data Warehouse 2.0 architecture (domain-driven, SCD Type 2, schema-based governance).
These conventions complement the core repository rules and naming conventions.

---

## Multi-File Consistency

If you update logic in `queries/**/*.sql`, you **must** automatically check and update the corresponding `metadata/**/*.yml` and `data_quality/**/*.yml` (layer folders: clean, enrich, dw, etc.).

---

## Target Schema Structure (DW 2.0)

Data is organized by functional domain for schema-level governance and access control:

| Schema | Scope |
|--------|-------|
| `dw_organization` | Cost centers, BUs, teams, job structure, Codex, business partners |
| `dw_employee_details` | PII, lifecycle events (admissions/exits), documentation, vacation, leaves, dependents, education |
| `dw_compensation` | Salary history, job level, pay-tables, merits/promotions, variable pay |
| `dw_sociodemographics` | DE&I data |
| `dw_performance` | Performance and talent cycles |
| `dw_people` | Public profile (name, email, hierarchy, location, role) |
| `dw_learning` | Learning & Development data |
| `dw_payroll` | Data from Payroll provider |
| `dw_hiring` | Talent Acquisition (TA) data |
| `dw_equity` | Equity data |
| `dw_survey` | Survey data |

When adding new tables, place them in the schema that matches the business domain.

